# Bustfile — Enaction Engine failure-mode contractile

@abstract:
Hard-stop failure modes for deterministic timing, identity, provenance, and
runtime/tooling boundaries.
@end

## Failure Modes

### partial-step-enters-simulation
- class: deterministic_integrity
- description: Host simulation observes a fractional render interval
- detection_probe: "cargo test --workspace"
- recovery: restore whole-step-only host integration and add a regression test
- status: declared

### interpolation-feeds-simulation
- class: deterministic_integrity
- description: A value sampled for rendering is written back into simulation state
- detection_probe: architecture review at every host integration
- recovery: separate completed simulation state from presentation views
- status: declared

### discontinuity-loses-fresh-state
- class: rendering_integrity
- description: snap is called without first committing the fresh discontinuous state
- detection_probe: "cargo test --workspace commit_then_snap"
- recovery: commit the fresh state, then snap, and preserve the regression test
- status: verified

### identity-drift
- class: repository_integrity
- description: Repository, crate, import, package, URL, or generated identity diverges from the canonical enaction namespace
- detection_probe: repository-wide identity search plus cargo metadata
- recovery: realign every identity surface without adding aliases
- status: declared

### speculative-subsystem
- class: architecture_integrity
- description: An empty crate or module claims an unimplemented engine facility
- detection_probe: workspace and source-tree review
- recovery: remove the facade; retain destination architecture in documentation until implemented and tested
- status: declared

### ums-runtime-cycle
- class: dependency_integrity
- description: Enaction Engine depends on UMS Studio or released games require the editor UI
- detection_probe: dependency and package-boundary review
- recovery: restore versioned profile/package contracts and optional adapter direction
- status: declared
